+### syrvis share declare / list
+
+Converge DSM shared folders to a declared payload; dump current share state.
+Full spec: [share-user-declare-spec.md](share-user-declare-spec.md).
+
+```bash
+<shares.json> | sudo syrvis share declare --json      # converge (create/assert/ACL)
+<shares.json> | sudo syrvis share declare --dry-run --json  # plan only
+sudo syrvis share list --json                          # current state (read-only)
+```
+
+**What declare does:**
+1. Validates a `syrvis-shares/v1` JSON payload from STDIN (frozen schema)
+2. Compares only the payload-named shares against DSM (blast-radius scoped)
+3. Creates missing plaintext shares, asserts hide-unauthorized/recycle-bin
+   posture, applies the principal→rw|ro ACL matrix (`"none"` = named removal)
+4. Re-reads and reports residual drift as JSON (`ok: false` + exit 1 if any)
+
+**Notes:**
+- Never deletes/renames/moves a share; unnamed ACL grants are reported, kept
+- Refuses to create encrypted shares (create-time human ceremony) and refuses
+  declared/actual encryption or volume contradictions
+- Root-only (DSM share API); over the seam it runs under `sudo -n`
+
+---
+
+### syrvis user declare / list
+
+Converge DSM local-user posture to a declared payload; dump the user database.
+Full spec: [share-user-declare-spec.md](share-user-declare-spec.md).
+
+```bash
+<users.json> | sudo syrvis user declare --json        # converge (create/shell/groups)
+<users.json> | sudo syrvis user declare --dry-run --json  # plan only
+sudo syrvis user list --json                          # current state (read-only)
+```
+
+**What declare does:**
+1. Validates a `syrvis-users/v1` JSON payload from STDIN (frozen schema)
+2. Creates missing users (`synouser --add` with a random, never-recorded
+   throwaway password — the credential ceremony stays human), asserts login
+   shells surgically, adds group memberships additively
+3. Re-asserts the seam accounts' `/bin/sh` shells in the SAME invocation
+   (any DSM user write regenerates `/etc/passwd` and would sever the seam)
+4. Re-reads and reports residual drift as JSON
+
+**Notes:**
+- NEVER touches passwords, never deletes/disables, never removes memberships
+- Refuses `administrators`/`docker` membership (root-equivalent — owner-only)
+
+---
+
+### syrvis seam verbs
+
+Emit the registered-verb catalog (the machine-readable seam contract).
+
+```bash
+syrvis seam verbs --json
+```
+
+**Notes:**
+- Read-only, no sudo; identical output to `python -m syrviscore.seam.gen verbs`
+- External tooling diffs this against its pinned expectation instead of
+  hardcoding call shapes; includes the stdin payload schemas
+
+---
+
 ### syrvis --version
 
 Display version information.
